  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Employment and particularly youth employment issues are at the centre of national development policies</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In Tanzania, youth unemployment remains a pressing challenge despite recent economic growth. The ILO is working with the Government of Tanzania, social partners, and other stakeholders to enhance job creation, particularly for young people and vulnerable groups, through targeted interventions and evidence-based policy support.

This initiative focuses on strengthening national capacities to develop and implement comprehensive employment policies, promoting decent work in rural areas, and fostering youth employment. The strategy includes revising the National Employment Policy, improving technical training institutions, and supporting employment-intensive approaches in infrastructure projects.

The ILO collaborates with government entities, including the Prime Minister&#x2019;s Office and local authorities, to coordinate youth employment initiatives, develop a monitoring framework, and expand green business opportunities. The expected outcomes include better employment prospects for young people, improved skills for labor market needs, and a sustainable, inclusive economy contributing to the achievement of the Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs).

Through these efforts, the ILO aims to advance productive employment, promote social justice, and support Tanzania&#x2019;s journey toward economic resilience and equitable growth.</narrative>
  </description>
